# 1. Release Readiness Checklist – Food Delivery App

Before releasing a new version of a Zomato/Swiggy-style app, QA should check the following:

* [ ] **Functional testing completed** – Main features like login, restaurant search, cart and ordering work correctly.
* [ ] **Payment testing completed** – UPI, cards and other supported payment methods work properly.
* [ ] **Order placement verified** – Users can successfully place an order and receive confirmation.
* [ ] **Regression testing completed** – Existing features still work after the new changes.
* [ ] **Critical and high-severity bugs resolved** – No major unresolved defect should block the release.
* [ ] **Performance testing completed** – Important screens should load within an acceptable time under normal conditions.
* [ ] **Different devices/platforms tested** – The app should work properly on supported Android/iOS versions and common screen sizes.
* [ ] **Notifications verified** – Order confirmation and status notifications should be generated correctly.
* [ ] **Security checks completed** – User and payment-related information should be handled safely.
* [ ] **Final build verification** – QA should test the exact build that is planned for production.

**Final decision:**
If the important test cases pass and there are no release-blocking defects, QA can recommend the build for release.

